## One Tree

The 132 Records in this folder are two disconnected forests: a tutorial of
chapters and ideas, and the project's own documents, sections and tasks. They
describe the same subjects twice, under two different link names, with no root.
This is the work of making them one tree — a single parent link from a single
root, branching out into named ideas, each idea surrounded by its own tasks.

**The tree is the reading order and the plan at once.** Walk it from the root
and you get the introduction, then the reason Lince exists, then each idea in
turn. Walk further down any branch and you reach the tasks that are left in it.
When a task lands, its text folds up into the prose of the idea it belonged to
and the task Record is deleted — so an idea's description thickens with what
was actually built, and what remains below it is always exactly what is left.

**Names are ideas, not coordinates.** A Record is called `Organ`, `Sync`,
`Karma`, `Condition` — never `TODO - Karma - 1.2`, never `(document)`, never a
chapter number. A name is what you link to; a coordinate is what you have to
look up.

**This folder is layered, not flat, and the layers disagree.** Transfer grew a
large set of features, then almost all of Lince was rewritten, then Transfer
grew again — so two passages about one subject can both be careful, considered
writing and still contradict each other, with nothing on the page saying which
one is later. Age is read from the history, never from where a passage sits in
a file: `Transfer - OLD STUFF DOWN HERE` is at position 1 and is among the
oldest text here.

**Nothing is discarded by the merge.** Every passage lands in exactly one of
four places, and only the first two are the merge's decision to make. Text that
is **stable** becomes the idea's prose. Text that is **superseded** — the same
need met another way since — is deleted, and the entry that deletes it names
what replaced it. Text that is merely **different** — not superseded, not
contradicted, just a stray idea whose vibe does not match the body of work
around it, like an observer on a Transfer, or "if this one resolves, mine
resolves too" — is not blended in and not dropped: it becomes its own backlog
Record hanging off the subject it belongs to. Text that **contradicts** what is
built is deleted if it is small, and kept as backlog with the contradiction
stated plainly if it is large or important enough to be worth reopening.

**The point of the fourth pile is that vibe is information.** Two things at the
same state that feel nothing alike should not sit in one list, because the list
stops being readable and the odd one gets skimmed past. Backlog is cheap and
individual cards are easy to throw away later; a good idea quietly absorbed
into a paragraph it does not belong in is not recoverable. When in doubt, it
becomes a card.

- [ ] **Two links, not five.** `@part-of [[Idea|uid]] n` for composition, with
      the number carrying sibling order, and `@reference` for everything
      sideways. `@chapter` stops being a parent predicate — the engine's
      "which predicate is this kind's parent" question disappears with it.
      Order is the number: decimals mean an insertion never renumbers siblings,
      and a depth-first walk from the root is the whole reading order.
- [ ] **State is the quantity and a Concept, kept in agreement.** The number is
      what sorts — the ladder is `1` stable, `0` backlog, `-1` todo, `-2`
      doing. The Concept is what the sand filters and colours. The Concept is
      derived from the number and never set against it; the checker refuses a
      file where the two disagree.
- [ ] **Add the state Concepts to the frozen list.** `@wip` is written in
      `tools/instinct/CONTRACT.txt` as the pair for `-2`, but it is not in
      `engine::instinct::VOCABULARY`, so `check_lingua.js` refuses it and no
      file here can say it. The contract documents something the folder cannot
      express. Decide the words, add them, then this task can carry its own.
- [ ] **A lossless gate before anything moves.** `check_lingua.js` checks
      structure only. `check_docs_lossless.js` compares against `docs/*.md`
      that no longer exists — five lines checked, one already missing. Snapshot
      every body at HEAD; after each step assert that every paragraph either
      still appears somewhere, or is listed with the pile it was triaged into
      and the reason. A deletion with no entry is a bug, not a judgement call.
- [ ] **Sort every Record by who wrote it, before anything is nested.** Prose
      that is Eduardo's is never rewritten, summarised or blended — it moves up
      to the head of its idea and the explanatory material attaches below it.
      Authorship does not follow depth: the tutorial ideas are written prose,
      while `Interfaceless - The Death of Lince` and the theory buried in
      `Transfer - OLD STUFF DOWN HERE` are his and sit at the bottom of
      documents.
- [ ] **Date the strata before merging a subject.** For each subject, establish
      from the git history which passages are later, and write the finding down
      where the merge can be checked against it. Transfer and Lince are the two
      that need this most: both were reworked more than once, and position in a
      file says nothing about age.
- [ ] **Triage every passage into one of four piles, and record which.**
      Stable, superseded, different, contradicting. A passage marked superseded
      names what replaced it. A passage marked different or contradicting
      becomes a backlog Record — `quantity: 0`, `@part-of` the subject it
      belongs to — never a paragraph folded into prose it does not fit. The
      lossless gate then checks the weaker promise that the merge can actually
      keep: every passage is either still present, or listed with its pile and
      its reason.
- [ ] **Split backlog cards by vibe, not by subject alone.** Two ideas at the
      same state that read nothing alike do not share a list. Prefer more small
      cards over one list that has to be skimmed — discarding a card later is
      one edit, and recovering an idea absorbed into the wrong paragraph is
      not possible.
- [ ] **Dissolve the documents into named ideas.** `Ontology` becomes `Record`,
      `Organ`, `Assertion`, `Concept`, `Lingua`, `Protein`, `Sync`, `Trail`,
      `Visibility`, `Proximity` — each one a noun worth linking to. `Karma`
      becomes `Condition`, `Threshold`, `Consequence`, `Frequency`. The
      singular/plural collisions (`Record`/`Records`, `Concept`/`Concepts`,
      `Transfer`/`Transfers`) resolve by merging, since the filename is the
      head and two Records cannot share one.
- [ ] **Retire the duplicate top-level Records** — `Karma (document)` into
      `Karma`, `Transfer (document)` into `Transfers` — keeping the surviving
      uid and rewriting every inbound link in place. Never by re-running the
      converter: its uids are hashes of the title, so a rename reads as 132
      deletions and 132 creations.
- [ ] **Promote a task to its own Record when it needs children.** A short list
      lives as checkboxes in the body of the idea it belongs to. A task that
      has to be broken down becomes a Record with a name of its own and its own
      children below it. Both shapes are the same tree.
- [ ] **Root the tree.** `First Steps` is the root and the only Record without
      a parent: the canvas, the sands, and a first taste of what Lince is for.
      Under it, first, the Death of Lince — why any of this exists. Then the
      ideas, each its own branch.
- [ ] **Rename the files last, in their own pass.** Merging and renaming in one
      commit is how a chapter was once destroyed while its six ideas kept
      pointing at a uid nothing claimed.
